<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
	Apple's privacy manifest. **Required**: since May 2024 App Store Connect
	rejects an upload whose bundle uses a "required reason" API without
	declaring why, and this app uses two of them.

	The two declarations below are not boilerplate — each names a specific call
	site, and if that call site goes away the declaration should go with it:

	  * UserDefaults — every settings type in `ArtscribeUI` (`Preferences`,
	    `Theme`, `RecentFiles`, `PracticeSettings`, `PrerollSettings`,
	    `InteractionSettings`, `SessionStore`). Reason **CA92.1**: read and write
	    information accessible only to this app. Nothing is shared with an app
	    group, and there is no group entitlement to share through.

	  * System boot time — `ProcessInfo.processInfo.systemUptime`, in
	    `ViewerModel+Playback` (the transport clock and the playback tick) and
	    `WaveformLanesView`. Reason **35F9.1**: measuring elapsed time between
	    events inside the app. It is a monotonic clock for the playhead, and the
	    value never leaves the process.

	Deliberately *absent*: the file-timestamp category. The app touches
	`FileManager` only for `fileExists`, `createDirectory`, `contentsOfDirectory`
	and `urls(for:)` — none of which read timestamps or metadata — so declaring
	it would claim an access that does not happen.

	Nothing is collected and nothing is tracked, which is the honest answer
	rather than a convenient one: the app makes no network calls, has no
	accounts, no analytics and no third-party SDKs. Audio never leaves the
	device. `NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes` is empty for the same reason, and the
	App Store Connect privacy questionnaire must be answered to match.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>
	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>CA92.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategorySystemBootTime</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>35F9.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
